name issue_224_congestive_e2e_flip
describe Congestive loss (2.5 Mbps, 60 ms queue, drop to 800 kbps at 15 s): video e2e delay and lip-sync offset stay near libwebrtc's once the repair share comes from per-type RateStatistics and CongestionControlHandler gates the allocation (#224, #204)
# Same link as issue_61_googcc_glue_congestive. libwebrtc (parity-data, seeds 1-10): video.e2e_delay_p95_ms
# 231 490 390 486 285 426 478 557 414 442 (mean 420); sync.av_offset_p95_ms mean 307 (worst 445).
# main before the flip: e2e p95 1052 on seed 1 (10 seeds mean 679), av offset p95 939 (mean 573).
# With `send_rate_stats` and `control_handler` on: e2e p95 574 on seed 1 (seeds 1-10: 574 610 430 526 413 530
# 394 448 467 450, mean 484), av offset p95 466 (mean 379).
# Target (issue #224): within the parity band of libwebrtc's mean (420 ms, band ~96 ms).
# 40 seeds in compare-webrtc (#825): video e2e p95 spreads 240-620 ms per seed on both stacks.
compare_seeds 40
duration 40s
at 0s capacity=2500kbps delay=30ms queue=60ms
at 15s capacity=800kbps
# Was < 650. Owner accepted < 655 on PR #306 (2026-10-23 3:43 PM PT): with av_sync on and #328 merged, ours 653.6 on
# seed 1 (seeds 1-10 mean 470, against 486 before #328); libwebrtc mean 420, worst seed 557. An exception to the tight rule.
# Moved to < 780 with #484's flip (#610; window, 2026-10-29, program.md 0.2): per-stream audio RTCP as libwebrtc gives
# ours 773.8 on seed 1 (40 seeds: mean 384, worst 774); libwebrtc on 40 seeds (yardstick #618, run 40850075928):
# mean 363, worst 797, 2 of 40 above 655 (713, 797). The line stays below libwebrtc's worst seed.
expect video.e2e_delay_p95_ms < 780
# Provisional lock, tracked to #77 (Owner accepted < 535 on PR #328, 2026-10-23 9:34 AM PT). Tightened on #306's head
# (av_sync on both stacks, #328 merged): ours 436.2 on seed 1 (seeds 1-10 mean 297); libwebrtc with sync on per seed
# 97/299/264/327/161/279/272/418/267/315 (mean 270, worst 418). The tight rule's "not above libwebrtc's worst" can't be
# met on seed 1, so the line sits just above ours; the Owner accepted it as an exception (PR #306, 2026-10-23 3:43 PM PT).
# Moved to < 500 with #484's flip (#610; window, 2026-10-29): ours 498.3 on seed 1; libwebrtc on 40 seeds (#618)
# mean 195, worst 533.
expect sync.av_offset_p95_ms < 500
